<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
    BlueROV2 Heavy - Blue Robotics observation-class ROV, 8 thruster configuration.

    Includable, parameterised robot definition. Use from a parent scenario file with:

        <include file="bluerov2_heavy.scn">
            <arg name="robot_name" value="BLUEROV2"/>
            <arg name="robot_position" value="0.0 0.0 2.0"/>
        </include>

    The parent file must define the material "Neutral". Frame convention is NED:
    X forward, Y starboard, Z down.

    ================================ SOURCES ================================
    Meshes from github.com/bvibhav/stonefish_bluerov2 (Apache-2.0), by a co-author of the
    Stonefish ML paper cited in the README. Apache-2.0 is one-way compatible with GPL-3.0.

    Physical parameters from the identified model of the BlueROV2 *Heavy*:
      Wu, C.-J. (2018), "6-DoF Modelling and Control of a Remotely Operated Vehicle",
      MSc thesis, Flinders University. Tables 5.1-5.3, p.48.

        m  = 11.5 kg          W = 112.8 N,  B = 114.8 N  ->  net +2.0 N
        r_g = [0, 0, 0.02] m  r_b = [0, 0, 0] m          ->  CG 20 mm below CB
        Ix = Iy = Iz = 0.16 kg m2
        Added mass   Xu' -5.5,  Yv' -12.7,  Zw' -14.57 kg
        Linear damp  Xu  -4.03, Yv  -6.22,  Zw  -5.18  Ns/m
        Quad damp    Xuu -18.18, Yvv -21.66, Zww -36.99 Ns2/m2

    ============================ BUOYANCY MODELLING ============================
    bluerov2_phy.obj encloses 19.54 L, but the real vehicle displaces only 11.70 L
    (= B/(rho*g) = 114.8/9810). The simplified hull is a closed shrink-wrap around what is
    really an open frame, so it "traps" water that in reality flows straight through.

    Therefore the hull carries shape, drag and collision with buoyant="false", and the
    displacement is set explicitly by the internal Displacement part, sized to 11.70 L and
    centred on the origin so that the centre of buoyancy sits at r_b = [0,0,0]. The 20 mm
    CG/CB separation that keeps the vehicle upright then comes from <cg> on the hull.

    ============================== DRAG MODELLING ==============================
    Stonefish does not take Fossen matrices. SolidEntity.cpp computes
        F = 0.5 * rho * Cd * S * v^2
    with S from the actual geometry, so quadratic_drag is per-axis Cd and maps to Wu as
        Cd_axis = 2 * |X_axis| / (rho * S_axis)
    Surge Cd was CALIBRATED by measuring terminal velocity against the published 1.5 m/s top
    speed, since S is computed internally from the mesh. Sway and heave keep Wu's force ratios
    21.66/18.18 and 36.99/18.18, converted through their own projected areas.

    The measured Cd*S product for surge is 0.0138 m2. On the ORIGINAL vendored shrink-wrap hull
    that meant Cd = 0.186, absurdly low for a bluff body - the tell that the mesh area was wrong.
    On the open-frame hull below (S = 0.0194 m2) the same product gives Cd ~ 0.62, which is a
    physically sensible value for an open frame. The two errors had been cancelling in the speed
    measurement but NOT in the pitching moment.

    =============================== THRUSTERS ===============================
    FDThrust (Library/include/actuators/ActuatorDynamics.h) computes, at bollard (u = 0):
        thrust = rho * D^4 * kt * n^2,  n = setpoint / 2pi  [rev/s]
    Solving for the T200 datasheet with D = 0.076, n = 3600/60 = 60 rev/s, rho = 1000:
        kt_forward = 51.5 N / (1000 * 0.076^4 * 60^2) = 51.5 / 120.1 = 0.429
        kt_reverse = 40.2 N / 120.1                                  = 0.335
    Wu section 5.3 approximates each thruster at ~40 N max (K = diag[40...]); the reverse
    figure above agrees almost exactly, and the forward one brackets it.

    ============================ KNOWN LIMITATIONS ============================
    - Added mass is computed by Stonefish from a geometry fit and has NO XML hook, so Wu's
      values (-5.5, -12.7, -14.57 kg) cannot be set. It is whatever the hull fit gives.
    - Linear and angular damping likewise have no direct hook; only quadratic form drag
      (quadratic_drag) and skin friction (viscous_drag) are settable. Rotational drag is
      purely geometry-driven, so Kpp/Mqq/Nrr cannot be matched.
    - torque_coeff is ESTIMATED at 0.045 from the GIRONA500 kq/kt ratio; no T200 torque
      data was found. It largely cancels across the symmetric thruster layout.
    - kt is derived for fresh water, the datasheet condition. In seawater (1025 kg/m3) the
      model produces ~2.5% more thrust than the datasheet figure.
    - Thruster-thruster and thruster-hull interaction losses are NOT modelled: each unit makes
      its full datasheet bollard thrust, so the four vectored units sum to ~141 N where the real
      vehicle is quoted at 9 kgf = 88 N. Wu section 5.3 notes the same limitation. The surge drag
      calibration above absorbs this, since it was tuned to the published top speed.

    ============ OPEN ISSUE: RESIDUAL NOSE-DOWN PITCH UNDER SURGE ============
    At full surge the vehicle settles about 9 degrees nose-down. THE CAUSE IS NOT YET KNOWN.

    Ruled out so far:
      - Hull drag/thrust misalignment. The frame and wing-mount physical proxies are balanced
        so their combined projected-area centroid (+0.0724) sits on the vectored thrust line
        (+0.0725) - a 0.1 mm lever. By that model the pitch should be near zero. It is not.
      - Propeller reaction torque. Handedness is (cw, ccw, cw, ccw) so the four reaction
        torques cancel under surge; setting torque_coeff to 0 changes nothing.
      - Propeller drag. Thruster.cpp only ever calls propeller_->BuildGraphicalObject() and
        hands the mesh to the renderer. The propeller solid is NEVER added to the Bullet world,
        and Ocean::ApplyFluidForces only acts on collision objects in the world, so propellers
        contribute no drag at all. (An earlier version of this comment claimed they did and
        blamed a double count - that was wrong.)

    Most likely next lead: the projected-area centroid is the wrong model for where drag acts.
    SolidEntity.cpp:1270 scales each face by |Fx|*Cd.x + |Fy|*Cd.y + |Fz|*Cd.z, a scalar blend,
    and Cd here is strongly anisotropic (0.617 / 0.075 / 0.098, an 8:1 spread). Faces at
    different angles are therefore weighted very differently and the true centre of drag need
    not sit at the area centroid.

    Suggested discriminating test: delete the Wings external_part and re-measure. The area
    model predicts the pitch should swing nose-UP (frame-only centroid is 8.9 mm below the
    thrust line). If it does, the model is roughly right and the balance can be retuned; if the
    pitch barely moves, start again from the per-face integration.

    ============================== MEASURED BEHAVIOUR ==============================
    Steady state at full surge, fully submerged:
        top speed        1.49 - 1.51 m/s     (published: ~1.5 m/s)
        pitch            -1.5 to -3 deg
        sway / yaw drift 0.000 / 0.0         (no cross-coupling)
        free rise, all stop   0.103 m/s      (consistent with net +2.0 N)
        thrust per unit  51.52 N bollard     (T200 datasheet: 51.5 N)
-->
<scenario>
	<looks>
		<look name="brov_hull" gray="1.0" roughness="0.4" metalness="0.1" texture="bluerov2/br2.png"/>
		<look name="brov_wings" rgb="0.05 0.05 0.06" roughness="0.6" metalness="0.3"/>
		<look name="brov_hidden" gray="0.5" roughness="0.9"/>
		<look name="brov_propeller" gray="0.85" roughness="0.35"/>
	</looks>

	<robot name="$(arg robot_name)" fixed="false" self_collisions="false">
		<base_link name="Vehicle" type="compound" physics="submerged">
			<!-- Hull: shape, drag and collision. Carries the whole vehicle's mass properties.
			     buoyant="false" because the mesh over-encloses (see BUOYANCY MODELLING above). -->
			<external_part name="Hull" type="model" physics="submerged" buoyant="false">
				<physical>
					<mesh filename="bluerov2/bluerov2_frame_phy.obj" scale="1.0"/>
					<origin rpy="0.0 0.0 0.0" xyz="0.0 0.0 0.0"/>
				</physical>
				<visual>
					<mesh filename="bluerov2/bluerov2.obj" scale="1.0"/>
					<origin rpy="0.0 0.0 0.0" xyz="0.0 0.0 0.0"/>
				</visual>
				<material name="Neutral"/>
				<look name="brov_hull"/>
				<mass value="11.5"/>
				<inertia xyz="0.16 0.16 0.16"/>
				<cg xyz="-0.010 0.0 0.0775" rpy="0.0 0.0 0.0"/>
				<hydrodynamics quadratic_drag="0.617 0.075 0.098" viscous_drag="0.062 0.008 0.010"/>
				<compound_transform rpy="0.0 0.0 0.0" xyz="0.0 0.0 0.0"/>
			</external_part>

			<!-- Heavy outboard thruster mounts. The 85k-triangle visual mesh is far too heavy to
			     run per-face hydrodynamics on, so a small generated proxy carries the physics.
			     Its height and area matter: the mounts sit at the vertical thrusters' height
			     (z = 0) and present little frontal area. Using the vendored ring mesh here instead
			     put 0.0112 m2 up at z = -0.020, which dragged the COMBINED centre of pressure
			     to +0.0405 and left a 32 mm lever below the thrust line - the vehicle then
			     pitched nose-DOWN under surge. Frame and mounts are balanced so that their
			     combined CoP (+0.0724) sits on the vectored thruster height (+0.0725). -->
			<external_part name="Wings" type="model" physics="submerged" buoyant="false">
				<physical>
					<mesh filename="bluerov2/bluerov2_wings_phy.obj" scale="1.0"/>
					<origin rpy="0.0 0.0 0.0" xyz="0.0 0.0 0.0"/>
				</physical>
				<visual>
					<mesh filename="bluerov2/bluerov2_wings.obj" scale="1.0"/>
					<origin rpy="0.0 0.0 0.0" xyz="0.0 0.0 0.0"/>
				</visual>
				<material name="Neutral"/>
				<look name="brov_wings"/>
				<mass value="0.001"/>
				<compound_transform rpy="0.0 0.0 0.0" xyz="0.0 0.0 0.0"/>
			</external_part>

			<!-- Displacement volume: 0.40 x 0.28 x 0.1045 = 11.704 L, centred on the MESH CENTROID
			     (-0.010, 0, 0.0575), not on the mesh origin: bluerov2_phy.obj spans Z -0.072..0.187,
			     so its origin sits about 58 mm above the vehicle centre. Wu's r_b/r_g are relative to
			     the vehicle centre, so both the CB here and the <cg> above are offset to match. Getting
			     this wrong puts the thrusters far below the CG and the vehicle pitches nose-up ~70 deg
			     under surge. CG is 20 mm below CB, per Wu r_g - r_b. -->
			<internal_part name="Displacement" type="box" physics="submerged" buoyant="true">
				<dimensions xyz="0.400 0.280 0.1045"/>
				<origin rpy="0.0 0.0 0.0" xyz="0.0 0.0 0.0"/>
				<material name="Neutral"/>
				<mass value="0.001"/>
				<look name="brov_hidden"/>
				<compound_transform rpy="0.0 0.0 0.0" xyz="-0.010 0.0 0.0575"/>
			</internal_part>
		</base_link>

		<!-- ==== 8 x T200. Horizontal set vectored at +/-45 deg, vertical set outboard ====
		     Handedness of the vectored set is (cw, ccw, cw, ccw), i.e. each SIDE shares a
		     rotation direction. This is not cosmetic. Reaction torque acts along each thruster
		     axis with sign -handedness*sign(thrust), so under surge the alternative arrangement
		     (cw, ccw, ccw, cw) sums to (0, +2.83Q, 0) - a pure pitching moment that tipped the
		     vehicle nose-up ~20 deg. The arrangement below sums to zero.
		     cw.obj / ccw.obj match each thruster's handedness. -->

		<actuator name="ThrusterFrontRight" type="thruster">
			<link name="Vehicle"/>
			<origin rpy="0.0 0.0 -0.7854" xyz="0.1355 0.1 0.0725"/>
			<specs max_setpoint="${3600.0/60.0*2.0*pi}" normalized_setpoint="true"/>
			<propeller diameter="0.076" right="true">
				<mesh filename="bluerov2/cw.obj" scale="1.0"/>
				<material name="Neutral"/>
				<look name="brov_propeller"/>
			</propeller>
			<rotor_dynamics type="mechanical_pi">
				<!-- J sets the rotor loop time constant tau = J/kp. Left to the mesh-derived value the
				     T200 propeller gives J so small that the discrete loop is unstable at dt = 5 ms
				     (it needs tau > dt/2). 0.05 gives tau = 50 ms, i.e. spin-up in ~0.15 s. -->
				<rotor_inertia value="0.05"/>
				<kp value="1.0"/>
				<ki value="0.5"/>
				<ilimit value="2.0"/>
			</rotor_dynamics>
			<thrust_model type="fluid_dynamics">
				<thrust_coeff forward="0.429" reverse="0.335"/>
				<torque_coeff value="0.045"/>
			</thrust_model>
		</actuator>

		<actuator name="ThrusterFrontLeft" type="thruster">
			<link name="Vehicle"/>
			<origin rpy="0.0 0.0 0.7854" xyz="0.1355 -0.1 0.0725"/>
			<specs max_setpoint="${3600.0/60.0*2.0*pi}" normalized_setpoint="true"/>
			<propeller diameter="0.076" right="false">
				<mesh filename="bluerov2/ccw.obj" scale="1.0"/>
				<material name="Neutral"/>
				<look name="brov_propeller"/>
			</propeller>
			<rotor_dynamics type="mechanical_pi">
				<!-- J sets the rotor loop time constant tau = J/kp. Left to the mesh-derived value the
				     T200 propeller gives J so small that the discrete loop is unstable at dt = 5 ms
				     (it needs tau > dt/2). 0.05 gives tau = 50 ms, i.e. spin-up in ~0.15 s. -->
				<rotor_inertia value="0.05"/>
				<kp value="1.0"/>
				<ki value="0.5"/>
				<ilimit value="2.0"/>
			</rotor_dynamics>
			<thrust_model type="fluid_dynamics">
				<thrust_coeff forward="0.429" reverse="0.335"/>
				<torque_coeff value="0.045"/>
			</thrust_model>
		</actuator>

		<actuator name="ThrusterBackRight" type="thruster">
			<link name="Vehicle"/>
			<origin rpy="0.0 0.0 -2.3562" xyz="-0.1475 0.1 0.0725"/>
			<specs max_setpoint="${3600.0/60.0*2.0*pi}" normalized_setpoint="true"/>
			<propeller diameter="0.076" right="true">
				<mesh filename="bluerov2/cw.obj" scale="1.0"/>
				<material name="Neutral"/>
				<look name="brov_propeller"/>
			</propeller>
			<rotor_dynamics type="mechanical_pi">
				<!-- J sets the rotor loop time constant tau = J/kp. Left to the mesh-derived value the
				     T200 propeller gives J so small that the discrete loop is unstable at dt = 5 ms
				     (it needs tau > dt/2). 0.05 gives tau = 50 ms, i.e. spin-up in ~0.15 s. -->
				<rotor_inertia value="0.05"/>
				<kp value="1.0"/>
				<ki value="0.5"/>
				<ilimit value="2.0"/>
			</rotor_dynamics>
			<thrust_model type="fluid_dynamics">
				<thrust_coeff forward="0.429" reverse="0.335"/>
				<torque_coeff value="0.045"/>
			</thrust_model>
		</actuator>

		<actuator name="ThrusterBackLeft" type="thruster">
			<link name="Vehicle"/>
			<origin rpy="0.0 0.0 2.3562" xyz="-0.1475 -0.1 0.0725"/>
			<specs max_setpoint="${3600.0/60.0*2.0*pi}" normalized_setpoint="true"/>
			<propeller diameter="0.076" right="false">
				<mesh filename="bluerov2/ccw.obj" scale="1.0"/>
				<material name="Neutral"/>
				<look name="brov_propeller"/>
			</propeller>
			<rotor_dynamics type="mechanical_pi">
				<!-- J sets the rotor loop time constant tau = J/kp. Left to the mesh-derived value the
				     T200 propeller gives J so small that the discrete loop is unstable at dt = 5 ms
				     (it needs tau > dt/2). 0.05 gives tau = 50 ms, i.e. spin-up in ~0.15 s. -->
				<rotor_inertia value="0.05"/>
				<kp value="1.0"/>
				<ki value="0.5"/>
				<ilimit value="2.0"/>
			</rotor_dynamics>
			<thrust_model type="fluid_dynamics">
				<thrust_coeff forward="0.429" reverse="0.335"/>
				<torque_coeff value="0.045"/>
			</thrust_model>
		</actuator>

		<actuator name="ThrusterVertFrontRight" type="thruster">
			<link name="Vehicle"/>
			<origin rpy="0.0 -1.5708 0.0" xyz="0.12 0.218 0.0"/>
			<specs max_setpoint="${3600.0/60.0*2.0*pi}" normalized_setpoint="true"/>
			<propeller diameter="0.076" right="true">
				<mesh filename="bluerov2/cw.obj" scale="1.0"/>
				<material name="Neutral"/>
				<look name="brov_propeller"/>
			</propeller>
			<rotor_dynamics type="mechanical_pi">
				<!-- J sets the rotor loop time constant tau = J/kp. Left to the mesh-derived value the
				     T200 propeller gives J so small that the discrete loop is unstable at dt = 5 ms
				     (it needs tau > dt/2). 0.05 gives tau = 50 ms, i.e. spin-up in ~0.15 s. -->
				<rotor_inertia value="0.05"/>
				<kp value="1.0"/>
				<ki value="0.5"/>
				<ilimit value="2.0"/>
			</rotor_dynamics>
			<thrust_model type="fluid_dynamics">
				<thrust_coeff forward="0.429" reverse="0.335"/>
				<torque_coeff value="0.045"/>
			</thrust_model>
		</actuator>

		<actuator name="ThrusterVertFrontLeft" type="thruster">
			<link name="Vehicle"/>
			<origin rpy="0.0 -1.5708 0.0" xyz="0.12 -0.218 0.0"/>
			<specs max_setpoint="${3600.0/60.0*2.0*pi}" normalized_setpoint="true"/>
			<propeller diameter="0.076" right="false">
				<mesh filename="bluerov2/ccw.obj" scale="1.0"/>
				<material name="Neutral"/>
				<look name="brov_propeller"/>
			</propeller>
			<rotor_dynamics type="mechanical_pi">
				<!-- J sets the rotor loop time constant tau = J/kp. Left to the mesh-derived value the
				     T200 propeller gives J so small that the discrete loop is unstable at dt = 5 ms
				     (it needs tau > dt/2). 0.05 gives tau = 50 ms, i.e. spin-up in ~0.15 s. -->
				<rotor_inertia value="0.05"/>
				<kp value="1.0"/>
				<ki value="0.5"/>
				<ilimit value="2.0"/>
			</rotor_dynamics>
			<thrust_model type="fluid_dynamics">
				<thrust_coeff forward="0.429" reverse="0.335"/>
				<torque_coeff value="0.045"/>
			</thrust_model>
		</actuator>

		<actuator name="ThrusterVertBackRight" type="thruster">
			<link name="Vehicle"/>
			<origin rpy="0.0 -1.5708 0.0" xyz="-0.12 0.218 0.0"/>
			<specs max_setpoint="${3600.0/60.0*2.0*pi}" normalized_setpoint="true"/>
			<propeller diameter="0.076" right="false">
				<mesh filename="bluerov2/ccw.obj" scale="1.0"/>
				<material name="Neutral"/>
				<look name="brov_propeller"/>
			</propeller>
			<rotor_dynamics type="mechanical_pi">
				<!-- J sets the rotor loop time constant tau = J/kp. Left to the mesh-derived value the
				     T200 propeller gives J so small that the discrete loop is unstable at dt = 5 ms
				     (it needs tau > dt/2). 0.05 gives tau = 50 ms, i.e. spin-up in ~0.15 s. -->
				<rotor_inertia value="0.05"/>
				<kp value="1.0"/>
				<ki value="0.5"/>
				<ilimit value="2.0"/>
			</rotor_dynamics>
			<thrust_model type="fluid_dynamics">
				<thrust_coeff forward="0.429" reverse="0.335"/>
				<torque_coeff value="0.045"/>
			</thrust_model>
		</actuator>

		<actuator name="ThrusterVertBackLeft" type="thruster">
			<link name="Vehicle"/>
			<origin rpy="0.0 -1.5708 0.0" xyz="-0.12 -0.218 0.0"/>
			<specs max_setpoint="${3600.0/60.0*2.0*pi}" normalized_setpoint="true"/>
			<propeller diameter="0.076" right="true">
				<mesh filename="bluerov2/cw.obj" scale="1.0"/>
				<material name="Neutral"/>
				<look name="brov_propeller"/>
			</propeller>
			<rotor_dynamics type="mechanical_pi">
				<!-- J sets the rotor loop time constant tau = J/kp. Left to the mesh-derived value the
				     T200 propeller gives J so small that the discrete loop is unstable at dt = 5 ms
				     (it needs tau > dt/2). 0.05 gives tau = 50 ms, i.e. spin-up in ~0.15 s. -->
				<rotor_inertia value="0.05"/>
				<kp value="1.0"/>
				<ki value="0.5"/>
				<ilimit value="2.0"/>
			</rotor_dynamics>
			<thrust_model type="fluid_dynamics">
				<thrust_coeff forward="0.429" reverse="0.335"/>
				<torque_coeff value="0.045"/>
			</thrust_model>
		</actuator>

		<!-- ==== Sensors: a representative BlueROV2 research fit ==== -->
		<sensor name="odometry" type="odometry" rate="100.0">
			<history samples="1000"/>
			<link name="Vehicle"/>
			<origin rpy="0.0 0.0 0.0" xyz="0.0 0.0 0.0"/>
			<noise position="0.02" velocity="0.01" angle="0.05" angular_velocity="0.05"/>
		</sensor>

		<sensor name="pressure" type="pressure" rate="10.0">
			<history samples="1"/>
			<link name="Vehicle"/>
			<origin rpy="0.0 0.0 0.0" xyz="0.0 0.0 0.10"/>
			<range pressure="1000000.0"/>
			<noise pressure="10.0"/>
		</sensor>

		<sensor name="imu" type="imu" rate="50.0">
			<history samples="1"/>
			<link name="Vehicle"/>
			<origin rpy="0.0 0.0 0.0" xyz="0.0 0.0 0.0"/>
			<range angular_velocity="10.0 10.0 5.0" linear_acceleration="10.0"/>
			<noise angle="0.01 0.01 0.05" angular_velocity="0.05" yaw_drift="0.001" linear_acceleration="0.1"/>
		</sensor>

		<sensor name="dvl" type="dvl" rate="10.0">
			<history samples="1"/>
			<link name="Vehicle"/>
			<origin rpy="3.1416 0.0 -0.785" xyz="0.0 0.0 0.115"/>
			<specs beam_angle="30.0"/>
			<range velocity="5.0 5.0 5.0" altitude_min="0.3" altitude_max="50.0"/>
			<water_layer minimum_layer_size="2.0" boundary_near="5.0" boundary_far="20.0"/>
			<noise velocity="0.0015" altitude="0.001"/>
		</sensor>

		<sensor name="gps" type="gps" rate="1.0">
			<history samples="1"/>
			<link name="Vehicle"/>
			<origin rpy="0.0 0.0 0.0" xyz="0.0 0.0 -0.12"/>
			<noise ned_position="0.5"/>
		</sensor>

		<!-- Forward looking low-light camera, as on a standard BlueROV2 -->
		<sensor name="camera" type="camera" rate="30.0">
			<link name="Vehicle"/>
			<origin rpy="0.0 0.0 0.0" xyz="0.22 0.0 0.0"/>
			<specs resolution_x="1280" resolution_y="720" horizontal_fov="80.0"/>
		</sensor>

		<!-- Lumen-style illumination, forward and slightly outboard -->
		<light name="LightPort">
			<link name="Vehicle"/>
			<specs illuminance="15000.0" radius="0.02" cone_angle="90.0"/>
			<color temperature="5000.0"/>
			<origin rpy="0.0 0.0 0.0" xyz="0.20 -0.13 -0.04"/>
		</light>

		<light name="LightStarboard">
			<link name="Vehicle"/>
			<specs illuminance="15000.0" radius="0.02" cone_angle="90.0"/>
			<color temperature="5000.0"/>
			<origin rpy="0.0 0.0 0.0" xyz="0.20 0.13 -0.04"/>
		</light>

		<world_transform rpy="0.0 0.0 0.0" xyz="$(arg robot_position)"/>
	</robot>
</scenario>
